node_modules

# IMAGE-NO-CREDENTIALS-1 — THE RUNTIME STORE NEVER ENTERS THE BUILD.
#
# `data/` holds this install's ACCOUNTS: users.json, users.json.bak-*, sessions.sqlite,
# setup-complete.json and recover-admin-audit.log, beside the seeded records. Until now the only
# line in this file was `node_modules`, so every one of those was sent to the Docker daemon as build
# context AND copied into the image by `COPY data/ ./data/`. Building on a used machine produced an
# image carrying the builder's password hashes — and, because `setup-complete.json` came with them,
# an image on which `POST /api/auth/setup` answers 409 forever, so a recipient could never create an
# admin and nothing would tell them why.
#
# NOTHING LEAKED: no image has ever been published. This closes it before the first one is.
#
# IGNORING IT HERE ALSO REMOVES THE COPY. A directory excluded from the context cannot be COPYed —
# the build would fail on a missing source — so the Dockerfile's `COPY data/ ./data/` had to go with
# it. That line was serving nothing: on a clean clone the whole tracked content of `server/data` is
# one README, and every directory the server needs under the data root is created at runtime with
# `mkdirSync(..., { recursive: true })`. Established by reading the tracked set and by booting an
# image built without it, not assumed.
data/
